-- title:
--   Labelled level automorphisms suffice to reach an Igusa disc
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$, a positive integer $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q$, i.e. with $q$ a non-unit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of the level-$M'$ $q$-expansion field `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, let `hle` be the inclusion of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` in `fieldBar q M'` = the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the function field of $X_H(q^2M')$ with $H = \ker(\mathrm{(ZMod}\,(q^2M'))^\times \to (\mathrm{ZMod}\,q)^\times)$, and let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $A$ with residue field `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`. Fix $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, a family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by the projective line over $\mathbb{Z}/q$, such that $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ consists exactly of the $f$ admitting Laurent series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal and $f\,y = x$ in Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ on `fieldBar q M'` with residue field `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2M') (levelH q M')` and with `R.integers` equal to $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$; a finite set $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of places of that residue field; and a map `disc` assigning to each such place a set of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Write $G$ for the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-automorphisms of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the level automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\zeta'$ arbitrary. It is assumed that every $\tau \in G$ preserving `R.integers` leaves $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ invariant under the induced residual automorphism `R.resAut τ`, and satisfies `RegularProlongation.smulDisc τ (disc Q) = disc (R.resAut τ • Q)` for all $Q \notin N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$. Call a place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` *untubed* if for no $s \in W$ does the following hold: for every $f$ in the integers of $R_0$ that is integral at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which the image of `jq` is integral, if the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$ then for every $a \in A$ with $\mathrm{residue}_A(a)$ equal to the value of $s$ at that residue, the difference between the value of $P$ at the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$. It is further assumed (`hδ`) that every untubed $P$ admits some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and some $Q \notin N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ • P ∈ disc Q`. Finally let $g$ assign to each $\ell$ in the projective line over $\mathbb{Z}/q$ an element of $G$ of the form `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and `redQ q γ • lineInfty q = ℓ`. The conclusion is that for every untubed place $P$ there are $\ell$ and $Q \notin N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ with `g ℓ • P ∈ disc Q`; that is, the chosen labelled automorphisms already realise the property asserted in `hδ` for arbitrary $\gamma$.
--
--   This is a bookkeeping step in the assembly of the semistable covering of the full-level modular curve $X_H(q^2M')$ by Igusa discs and supersingular tubes: it replaces the arbitrary element of $\Gamma_0(M')$ produced by the tube/disc dichotomy with one of the finitely many automorphisms labelled by the points of the projective line over $\mathbb{Z}/q$. It is used in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted).
